                                "sense_id": "e35245b5-4d86-372a-87b7-d4e43daae2d9",
                                "text": "The springs are so few in number that their names are household words in every Indian rancheria and every settler's home; and there are no brooks, no creeks, and no rivers but the trunk of the Colorado and the trunk of the Gila."
